@index
Templates — the CTAN document classes, imported as one phextura corpus.

Every document class enumerated on the CTAN class topic page was imported from the pre-packaged TeX Live distribution archives (never scraped package by package). Each template Book holds a header scroll (class, package, version, license, mechanically extracted structure: declared options and sectioning commands) followed by the class's source files verbatim.

Enumerated: 449 packages. Templates: 595. Gaps: 51.

For LaTeX users — where the familiar things live here:
If you learned LaTeX from the usual first tutorial (cited under References below), you already know this corpus's shape. The journey that tutorial walks maps onto a phextura paper like this:
  document: one phextura corpus instead of one .tex stream — its parts are scrolls, each holding one block (a paragraph, an equation, a theorem).
  class: the templates in this corpus. In LaTeX you write \documentclass{...}; here a paper names a style scroll from Collection 4 (styles), and each template Book below is one class exactly as CTAN ships it — header first, in your vocabulary: documentclass options, the sectioning ladder, the environments it provides — then its source, verbatim.
  preamble: a paper's Collection 6 (metadata) scrolls and its style choices — the setup lives at stated addresses rather than above \begin{document}.
  title, author, abstract: Collection 6 (metadata) scrolls of the paper.
  sections: the sectioning ladder is the paper's own coordinates — a section is an address (Chapter.Section.Scroll inside its Book), not only a command in a stream.
  figures: Collection 3 (media). One float is one object at one address; its caption travels with it, and a reference is that address — nothing dangles and nothing needs a second pass to settle.
  tables: the same treatment as figures — an addressed block, captioned and referenced by its coordinate.
  mathematics: equation blocks in the body, addressed like every other block.
  bibliography: Collection 2 — one reference entry per scroll; the short citation key you type resolves to a durable address underneath.
Where phextura deliberately differs, with its reasons stated plainly:
  addressed scrolls instead of one file — so structure can be read without executing macros, and references resolve by construction rather than by rerun.
  standoff notes instead of marginal floats (\marginpar and friends) — a note pins to an address outside the paper and cannot drift away from its sentence; the paper itself is never modified by its annotations.
  classes as cited, preserved sources — each template here carries its package, version and license, because a class in phextura is a scroll a paper addresses, not a file a filename search happens to find.

References:
reference: Learn LaTeX in 30 minutes — Overleaf (online tutorial).
url: https://www.overleaf.com/learn/latex/Learn_LaTeX_in_30_minutes
summary (in our own words; the tutorial is cited, not reproduced): a first-document walkthrough for complete beginners. It begins with a minimal file that already typesets, then grows it piece by piece: declaring the document class with \documentclass; the preamble as the document's setup region, where class options such as font and paper size are given and packages are loaded; title, author and date declared in the preamble and printed in the body, followed by the abstract environment; plain text formatting and comments; dividing the body with the sectioning ladder (part and chapter in book-like classes, then section down to subparagraph) and generating a table of contents; inserting graphics and wrapping them as figures with captions, labels and cross-references; lists; mathematics both inline and displayed, through to fuller examples; building tables with the tabular environment, again captioned, labelled and referenced; and it closes with how packages are found on CTAN and distributed through TeX Live — the same pre-packaged distribution this corpus was harvested from. Bibliography management is named up front among the facilities LaTeX offers; the walkthrough itself ends at packages and CTAN, pointing onward.

